WEBVTT

00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:11,500
Here's another book for my grandkids called Matilda Brown.

00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:19,980
One day, not very long ago, beside a quiet town, there was a woman rather large, her name

00:00:19,980 --> 00:00:22,020
Matilda Brown.

00:00:22,020 --> 00:00:31,860
Her home was just a cottage, crooked, chipped, and bent, with a porch made of cedar wood,

00:00:31,860 --> 00:00:37,690
worn gray, and spent.

00:00:37,690 --> 00:00:46,770
She baked every Monday a few brown loafs of bread, a white cake that she'd give to bless

00:00:46,770 --> 00:00:55,450
someone, she said, a pie for her dessert after dinners for the week, a turkey that she'd

00:00:55,450 --> 00:01:00,010
share with someone new that she would seek.

00:01:00,010 --> 00:01:07,410
She looked not for a thank you, as her blessings she'd bestow, she just said, my debt was

00:01:07,410 --> 00:01:13,670
paid so very long ago.

00:01:13,670 --> 00:01:21,170
On Tuesdays, she'd sit and sketch with a pencil on her chair, as she rocked her mind

00:01:21,170 --> 00:01:25,250
with water, and mentally prepare.

00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:33,410
For this day she compiled a list of the ones that she would bless, for the postman, her

00:01:33,410 --> 00:01:42,700
pastor, neighbor, or a stranger was best.

00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:49,140
The evening was for writing cards, just to make one smile.

00:01:49,140 --> 00:01:55,660
She would decorate them with antique lace, and put them in a pile.

00:01:55,660 --> 00:02:02,980
One by one she blessed them with a prayer, for those who'd soon receive, a little piece

00:02:02,980 --> 00:02:07,500
of heaven, to help them to believe.

00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:15,740
She looked not for a thank you, as her blessings she'd bestow, she just said, my debt was paid

00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:21,860
so very long ago.

00:02:21,860 --> 00:02:29,700
For on Wednesdays she'd travel, with a cane in one hand, at her bag filled with trickets

00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:32,380
she'd wrapped with a band.

00:02:32,380 --> 00:02:39,340
Some cards of thanksgiving, a sandwich or two, homemade angels of popsicle sticks held

00:02:39,340 --> 00:02:50,260
with glue, some leftover cookies on plates wrapped in foil, white cake, now frosted, and

00:02:50,260 --> 00:02:55,140
six colored eggs, hard boiled.

00:02:55,140 --> 00:03:02,940
Distributing treasures on Wednesdays, she'd say, was where I was most blessed when I gave

00:03:02,940 --> 00:03:05,220
away.

00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:13,340
She looked not for a thank you, as her blessings she'd bestow, she just said, my debt was paid

00:03:13,340 --> 00:03:18,760
so very long ago.

00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:25,720
Thursdays you'd think she'd be tired of her tolls, but the woman woke early to gather some

00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:27,480
bowls.

00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:34,440
She filled them half full with some cream, mix some milk mixed with cream, then she put on

00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:40,290
her apron that was stained at the seam.

00:03:40,290 --> 00:03:48,770
Now carefully placing the bowls on a tray she paused, bowed her head and thankfully prayed.

00:03:48,770 --> 00:03:56,770
With both wrinkled hands and a shake in her step, she carried those meals made for strays

00:03:56,770 --> 00:03:58,770
with some pep.

00:03:58,770 --> 00:04:05,130
She kicked the screen door open, crossed the porch, down the stairs, passed the path to the

00:04:05,130 --> 00:04:14,730
shed where she once kept the mirrors, set, she set each separate bowl with precision and

00:04:14,730 --> 00:04:20,290
love for a hungry young kitten she was sent from above.

00:04:20,290 --> 00:04:26,810
She coaxed them with breakfast, each Thursday they'd say, and hopes to save one from the fate

00:04:26,810 --> 00:04:28,650
of a stray.

00:04:28,650 --> 00:04:35,570
She looked not for a thank you as her blessings she'd bestow, she just said, my debt was paid

00:04:35,570 --> 00:04:41,100
so very long ago.

00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:47,900
Fridays she would walk the 12 blocks into town where the animal shelter took her rescued

00:04:47,900 --> 00:04:54,940
on down by the bus to the metro where people would pay for the kiddies and puppies they'd

00:04:54,940 --> 00:04:58,620
bring there that day.

00:04:58,620 --> 00:05:06,220
In a way she was a savior to that gentle lot who knew little of their dangers nor of her

00:05:06,220 --> 00:05:08,740
protective plot.

00:05:08,740 --> 00:05:17,740
She was said that Fridays were her favorite day for reminded her of just what her savior

00:05:17,740 --> 00:05:19,580
had paid.

00:05:19,580 --> 00:05:26,660
She looked not for a thank you as her blessings she'd bestow, she just said, my debt was paid

00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:30,650
so very long ago.

00:05:30,650 --> 00:05:37,370
Saturdays were days of rest for many in the town, but as you'd guess our kind old friend didn't

00:05:37,370 --> 00:05:39,610
let that get her down.

00:05:39,610 --> 00:05:47,810
She woke it down to hit the market before the sun was hot and pipped the freshest vegetables

00:05:47,810 --> 00:05:52,560
to boil in a pot.

00:05:52,560 --> 00:06:01,320
At home she'd add the chicken, carrots, beans and rice, then while she'd make some buns

00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:05,840
it cooked and she'd add her secret spice.

00:06:05,840 --> 00:06:13,520
As she invited special guests some people in the know, no there were others in her mind

00:06:13,520 --> 00:06:18,980
and she was sure they'd show.

00:06:18,980 --> 00:06:26,060
But always done she mustered up a will too strong to ignore and loved that giant pot of

00:06:26,060 --> 00:06:29,540
soup across the kitchen floor.

00:06:29,540 --> 00:06:35,940
She kicked the screen door open across the porch down the stairs, passed the path to the

00:06:35,940 --> 00:06:39,460
shed where she once kept the mayors.

00:06:39,460 --> 00:06:48,460
She placed the pot of blessings on a stump just perfect height, then begged to call the passers-by

00:06:48,460 --> 00:06:53,720
to come taste her delight.

00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:58,760
She fed the children down the block whose daddy had no work.

00:06:58,760 --> 00:07:03,800
She fed the couple on their walk though it was just a perk.

00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:11,680
She fed a little puppy, a man from out of town and others that had need came, for word

00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:14,080
had spread around.

00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:17,200
Some took as if expected.

00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:25,000
Some thanked her with a smile, some needed it so badly, others stayed to talk a while.

00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:29,400
She looked not for a thank you as her blessings she'd bestow.

00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:36,390
She just said my dad was paid so very long ago.

00:07:36,390 --> 00:07:41,030
Sunday was a day of rest after church was done.

00:07:41,030 --> 00:07:46,710
There she attended Bible school and learned about such fun.

00:07:46,710 --> 00:07:51,150
She smiled as new ideas would pop into her head.

00:07:51,150 --> 00:07:57,550
She learned of how to be a blessing from the master as she read.

00:07:57,550 --> 00:08:02,270
Some others talked about her as they chatted about the town.

00:08:02,270 --> 00:08:08,910
I heard a young girl say once, I want to be like until the brown.

00:08:08,910 --> 00:08:16,110
If Mrs. Brown could hear she'd smile and tell her, lassie as you grow, just remember that

00:08:16,110 --> 00:08:20,470
your dad was paid so very long ago.

